    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2Y3xmjsAnfiFFL5PXxphuVh)_\n\n`M-x yadm` (and any first use of Magit) failed with `Given parent class emacsql-sqlite-connection is not a class`. The backtrace shows `magit` → `forge` → `code-review` (`:after forge`) → `code-review-db`, and the class is still missing even after `(require 'emacsql-sqlite)`.\n\n- `code-review` is now `:defer t` with `:commands`, so it loads only when a review starts. A broken `code-review` can no longer break Magit, Forge or `yadm`.\n- Removed the `:after forge` and the `require` that did not help.\n- Updated `docs/tangles/prog/sp-vcontrol.org` (tangled `.el` kept in sync), `docs/architecture/load-order.org` and `CHANGELOG.org`.\n\nNot run in Emacs (none in the container). The likely cause, `code-review` out of step with the installed `emacsql`/`closql`, is not confirmed. If the review commands still fail with the same message, run `M-x elpaca-update-all`, pin `emacsql`/`closql`, or drop the block (steps are in the doc).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiACqkAJPZmg4bMjzv1)_",
